1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
This lesson maintains an
existing IC command board in a

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,200
fictional warehouse exercise.

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:09,600
The screens come from the same saved
exercise across browser sessions.

4
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:13,200
Begin in Call Details and
verify the Warehouse alarm

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:14,800
name and training location.

6
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:18,400
Active Command and Open Command
Board identify the available

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,000
route into this incident.

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,600
Choose Open Command Board.

9
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:25,600
Check the incident name again
on Command Board, along with

10
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:27,200
Wallace Boden as commander.

11
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:31,600
Before practicing, make this identity
check a habit; similar lane names

12
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,600
can appear on different incidents.

13
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:36,400
Command Structure shows
Search Division and Staging.

14
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:41,200
Squad 3 is already in Search Division;
Staging has no assigned resource.

15
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:45,200
Rotate and Requirements are review
cues on the saved assignment.

16
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:48,000
They do not move the unit automatically.

17
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,200
Scroll to Resources.

18
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:53,200
All is selected, with Unassigned
and Assigned available beside it.

19
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:58,400
The pool contains Squad 3, Engine 51
and the fictional Exercise Gate Marshal.

20
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:03,600
Engine 51 names Christopher Herrmann in
its Officer or Team Lead position while

21
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:06,400
the unit remains unassigned to a lane.

22
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:09,600
Crew membership and command
allocation describe different things.

23
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:13,200
For practice, explain that
difference before proposing a move.

24
00:01:13,200 --> 00:01:15,200
In Tactical Objectives, choose Add.

25
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:18,800
The empty section gives
us a clear starting point.

26
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:23,200
In Add Objective, select Benchmark
under Type and enter the training

27
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,000
primary-search objective.

28
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Choose Add to save it.

29
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,800
A specific objective name gives the next
operator something concrete to review.

30
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:34,800
Open the objective and use
Progress to set fifty percent.

31
00:01:34,800 --> 00:01:37,600
The returned details show
fifty percent selected.

32
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:40,800
Outcome, Close-out note and
Complete Objective describe a

33
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:42,000
separate close-out decision.

34
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,400
This exercise leaves the
objective incomplete.

35
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:47,200
Practice updating progress
without treating an estimate

36
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:48,800
as a completed search.

37
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:52,800
In the Needs section,
use Add to open Add Need.

38
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,400
Choose Medical under Category.

39
00:01:54,400 --> 00:02:00,000
Enter the training rehab need, set
Qty to two, and use Details to explain

40
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,400
the gap: two fictional rehab positions
at staging, for internal tracking.

41
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:07,600
Choose Add after checking
the name and quantity.

42
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:12,400
This example records a quantified
need; it does not request a provider

43
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:14,000
or demonstrate anyone arriving.

44
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,600
Open the saved need.

45
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:20,800
Its heading still shows an open
medical need with zero of two filled.

46
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:24,800
For practice, describe what remains
outstanding before entering a fill.

47
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:28,800
In the need details,
set Fill to one of two.

48
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:34,000
Enter an explicit training explanation
in Note or Reason, then choose Save Fill.

49
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The number is a tracking entry; it is not
evidence of a person reaching staging.

50
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,200
Reopen the need.

51
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:45,600
Partial Fill and one of two
now describe the saved result.

52
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:50,400
History attributes the change to Wallace
Boden and retains the training reason.

53
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:56,800
The board also shows the need at one of
two beside the objective at fifty percent.

54
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,800
Leave the remaining gap visible.

55
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:02,800
For practice, explain why a partial
fill should remain distinguishable

56
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,200
from completing or closing the need.

57
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:08,000
Scroll to Notes and choose Add Note.

58
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,600
Give the next operator a
concrete location and scope.

59
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:16,400
Our note keeps staging at the
fictional west gate and explicitly says

60
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:18,400
there is no operational deployment.

61
00:03:18,400 --> 00:03:20,000
Under Visibility, select Internal.

62
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:24,400
The helper says the note is
visible to command staff only

63
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:29,200
and that the log records who
added it, rather than its text.

64
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:31,200
Public is a different choice.

65
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:34,000
Check the intended
audience, then choose Save.

66
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:38,800
After reopening the board, the note
retains its Internal badge and body.

67
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:43,200
Below it, ICS Role Assignments names
Matthew Casey as Safety Officer.

68
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:47,200
That existing command role is
separate from a unit riding

69
00:03:47,200 --> 00:03:48,800
position or lane assignment.

70
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:53,200
Practice checking the note audience
before using a shared command device.

71
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:57,600
Timers and PAR shows the existing
Training PAR reminder as overdue,

72
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:58,800
with Acknowledge available.

73
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:02,400
Its elapsed time reflects the
saved exercise across sessions.

74
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:05,600
This recording does not
acknowledge or restart it.

75
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:10,400
A reminder needs a deliberate operational
response; its badge alone says nothing

76
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,400
about a crew member's condition.

77
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,600
Now read Accountability.

78
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:18,400
The call says check-in timers are
active, but no timers are configured.

79
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:22,400
Refresh is visible, but this empty
configuration cannot demonstrate a

80
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,800
successful check-in or a PAR result.

81
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:28,400
For practice, explain which
information is missing before asking

82
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:31,200
a crew to rely on this display.

83
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:36,400
On Incident Map, check the actual
Chicago street map and Squad 3 marker

84
00:04:36,400 --> 00:04:38,400
with its Search Division label.

85
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:42,800
These are fictional training positions,
not a demonstration of device GPS.

86
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:46,800
Pan to frame the surrounding
streets, then choose Save View.

87
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:51,600
Here the manual pan moves the
marker to the right of center.

88
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:54,400
Reopening the incident
map retains that framing.

89
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:57,200
A full browser reload retains it too.

90
00:04:57,200 --> 00:05:01,200
Pan and Save View were
verified in this web recording.

91
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:06,000
Line, Area and Text are visible, but
annotation placement was not verified.

92
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Native touch, location and offline
behavior need separate device checks.

93
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Practice saving a useful view
and checking the returned map.

94
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,600
Return to the board and
scroll to Incident Log.

95
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:21,600
Read the timestamped objective addition,
progress update and need-fill entry.

96
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:24,800
They connect the working
cards to attributed actions.

97
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:29,600
The internal note has a non-public
log marker with its author; its

98
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:32,400
body stays out of this log entry.

99
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:36,000
The map-created entry is
also present after Save View.

100
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:40,400
For handover practice, compare this
history with the saved cards, identify

101
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:45,200
the remaining one-of-two gap, and state
that the objective is still incomplete.

102
00:05:45,200 --> 00:05:47,200
Leave this training command active.

103
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:52,000
This lesson verifies recorded application
state; it does not establish a field

104
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,800
deployment, delivered notification
or completed accountability check.

